            "review_text": "WanderWonderLife\nRiga, Latvia18 contributions\n0\nBia Hoi Hanoi and jungle decor\nOct 2017 • Couples\nI was initially intrigued by the spiral wood staircase with hanging plant-vines and waterfalls cascading behind the stairs, as well as the top floors with a multitude of green, hanging plants as frames for this bamboo-built restaurant. \nI was even more pleasantly surprised by the seamless transition from a waterfall staircase to the eating area reminiscent of being in a bamboo cabin in a jungle. \nThe service was fantastic-a series of three people, through short verbal cues, led my husband and I to a corner table on the top floor with a view. \nWe were immediately given a menu by a smiling waitress eager to take our order, and eager to please. Bonus-menu in English and Vietnamese!\nThis place has Bia Hoi Hanoi (bottled) for 15000 VND, a fair and decent price, and the food we ordered was an assortment of typical Vietnamese vegetarian fare, all delicious. \nWe didn't have to wait long for our food, and the ambience was just perfect. \nPeople were laughing and having a good time, but no one was too loud, nor was it too quiet. \nThis is a great place for big parties or celebrations, as they have hotpots to share, and long wooden tables to accommodate many guests in large groups. They equally have small tuckered-away tables for the occasional couple like ourselves. \nI would highly recommended eating here. \n\n*One improvement that could be made is the bathrooms-they were not so clean, doors didn't close and/or lock, and the hand-washing sink was clogged and dirty.\nRead more\nWritten October 14, 2017",
