            "review_text": "Leean W\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam206 contributions\n0\nOne of the Best Vietnamese Restaurants in Town\nFeb 2017 • Friends\nI have been to Rum Quan on several occasions, usually with a large group of friends which all adds to the ambience. It's quite a way out in Cau Gia but well worth the effort. Rum Quan is a large place on several floors but a very pleasant surprise indoors. It's always packed with people, adding to the vibrant atmosphere and has a very natural, rural, ethnic feel to it, with palm leaf roofs and ceilings, waterfalls, natural wood tables and chairs, hand woven mats etc. There are mainly Vietnamese customers but foreigners can enjoy the real Vietnamese atmosphere of everyone enjoying themselves and the frequent toasts going on in Vietnamese never fail to delight me. There is now a menu in English as well as Vietnamese and they serve beer as well as soft drinks and rice wine although I don't think they sell wine by the glass. The food is standard Vietnamese home cooking style cuisine - such as squid, pigs ears and heart etc but for the less adventurous like me there are plenty of delicious veggie dishes - such as chayote - a delicious leafy green Vietnamese vegetable, hot fried pickled cabbage - the big green leaf sort not the western small purple pickle - and fried sweet corn, thin egg noodles with thin beef and green vegetables and much more. Go to experience the true Vietnamese cooking and atmosphere, and although each level gets more and more beautiful as you ascend, the best atmosphere and welcome is on floor 1 where every table is packed and everyone is completely enjoying themselves with gusto.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten February 15, 2017",
